[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#F5A623]OVERVIEW[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

O'DailyQuests is a powerful, highly configurable quest system for survival, RPG, and network servers. Give every player short-term objectives, longer weekly challenges, and meaningful monthly goals — all from one plugin.

Run [B]Daily[/B], [B]Weekly[/B], and [B]Monthly[/B] quests at the same time, or enable only the periods that fit your server. Each period is a complete quest system of its own, with separate quest pools, progress, reset schedules, rerolls, quest counts, and rewards.

For example, you can give players [B]3 Daily quests[/B], [B]8 Weekly quests[/B], and [B]4 Monthly quests[/B] simultaneously. Completing or resetting one period never affects another.

This resource is an independently maintained [B]GPL-3.0 continuation[/B] of [URL='https://github.com/Ordwen/ODailyQuests']Ordwen's archived ODailyQuests[/URL]. The original plugin and design were created by Ordwen. Version 4.5 is maintained by LucidAPs for modern Paper servers.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55FFAA] DAILY • WEEKLY • MONTHLY [/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B]Three independent quest periods in one familiar system[/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

Every period has its own:

✅ Easy, Medium, Hard, Global, and custom quest pools
✅ Configurable number of active quests per category
✅ Player progress and active quest selection
✅ Reset timer and schedule
✅ Reroll allowance and reroll history
✅ Category-completion rewards
✅ All-quests-completed reward
✅ Lifetime completed-quest total

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]INDEPENDENT RESET SCHEDULES[/COLOR][/B]

✅ Daily — Choose the reset time and timezone
✅ Weekly — Choose the weekday, reset time, and timezone
✅ Monthly — Choose the day of the month, reset time, and timezone
✅ Supports global scheduled resets and player-relative renewal mode
✅ Short months automatically use their final valid day

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]SEPARATE QUEST FILES[/COLOR][/B]

[CODE]plugins/ODailyQuests/quests/
├── easy.yml
├── medium.yml
├── hard.yml
├── global.yml
├── weekly/
│   ├── easy.yml
│   ├── medium.yml
│   ├── hard.yml
│   └── global.yml
└── monthly/
    ├── easy.yml
    ├── medium.yml
    ├── hard.yml
    └── global.yml[/CODE]

Daily Easy and Weekly Easy are completely different pools. The same separation applies to every category, including Global quests.

[B]Global quest behavior has not changed.[/B] Each period simply loads Global quests from its own folder, so Daily Global, Weekly Global, and Monthly Global remain fully independent.

Existing installations keep their current filenames. Servers using [B]easyQuests.yml[/B], [B]mediumQuests.yml[/B], [B]hardQuests.yml[/B], and [B]globalQuests.yml[/B] receive the same naming convention in the new period folders without renaming their files.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55AAFF]✨ KEY FEATURES ✨[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

✅ Enable Daily, Weekly, and Monthly quests in any combination
✅ YAML, SQLite, or MySQL storage with UUID-based player tracking
✅ Easy, Medium, Hard, Global, and fully custom quest categories
✅ More than 20 built-in quest types with dynamic and random objectives
✅ Per-period quest counts, progress, rerolls, timers, and rewards
✅ Per-quest, per-category, all-completed, and lifetime milestone rewards
✅ Conditional and permission-based quests
✅ World, region, and category restrictions
✅ Anti-abuse checks for placed, broken, and dropped items
✅ Titles, subtitles, toasts, boss bars, action bars, chat feedback, and progress bars
✅ Period-aware player GUI with configurable Daily, Weekly, and Monthly navigation
✅ Custom heads, PlaceholderAPI content, Nexo items, model data, and item models
✅ Synchronized progression for matching objectives
✅ Safety mode, configurable command aliases, and storage conversion tools
✅ Multi-server friendly player-data delay and asynchronous SQL work
✅ Editable messages with HEX colors
✅ Custom quest types for manual or scripted completion with [B]/dqa customcomplete[/B]

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55FFAA] LIFETIME TOTALS & LEADERBOARDS [/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B]Keep the original overall total while tracking every period separately[/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

Every player now has four lifetime completion totals:

✅ Overall total across Daily + Weekly + Monthly
✅ Daily lifetime total
✅ Weekly lifetime total
✅ Monthly lifetime total

Existing totals remain fully backwards compatible. [CODE]%odailyquests_total%[/CODE], existing total commands, and the all-time leaderboard continue to use the player's [B]combined overall total[/B].

Create holograms, scoreboards, menus, chat formats, or NPC displays without a separate leaderboard addon:

[CODE]%odailyquests_total_1_alltime_name%[/CODE]
Returns the name of the player at rank 1. Replace [B]1[/B] with any positive position.

[CODE]%odailyquests_total_1_alltime_value%[/CODE]
Returns that ranked player's combined lifetime completed-quest total.

[CODE]%odailyquests_total_position%[/CODE]
Returns the viewing player's current all-time rank.

✅ Works with [B]YAML, SQLite, and MySQL[/B]
✅ Includes persisted offline-player totals and current active-player progress
✅ Uses a short cache so scoreboards can request rankings efficiently
✅ Deterministic ranking order for tied totals

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#F5A623]PLACEHOLDERAPI[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

Use [B]daily[/B], [B]weekly[/B], or [B]monthly[/B] in period-specific placeholders:

[CODE]%odailyquests_daily_total%
%odailyquests_weekly_total%
%odailyquests_monthly_total%

%odailyquests_daily_achieved%
%odailyquests_weekly_drawin%
%odailyquests_monthly_name_1%
%odailyquests_weekly_progress_1%
%odailyquests_daily_progressbar_1%
%odailyquests_weekly_total_easy%[/CODE]

Period prefixes also work with quest status, completion, required amount, description, and category placeholders. Existing unqualified placeholders remain supported for backwards compatibility.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#F5A623]QUEST TYPES[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]BLOCKS & ITEMS[/COLOR][/B]
✅ BREAK — Break blocks
✅ PLACE — Place blocks
✅ GET / PICKUP — Obtain or pick up items
✅ CRAFT — Craft items
✅ COOK — Extract cooked items
✅ ENCHANT — Enchant items
✅ FISH — Catch items while fishing
✅ FARMING — Harvest mature crops
✅ CONSUME — Eat, drink, or use consumables
✅ LAUNCH — Launch projectiles
✅ CARVE — Carve pumpkins

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]ENTITIES & PLAYER ACTIONS[/COLOR][/B]
✅ KILL — Kill mobs or players
✅ TAME / BREED / SHEAR / MILKING — Animal objectives
✅ FIREBALL_REFLECT — Reflect a fireball
✅ VILLAGER_TRADE — Complete matching villager trades
✅ LOCATION — Reach configured coordinates
✅ EXP_POINTS / EXP_LEVELS — Earn experience
✅ PLAYER_DEATH — Track player deaths
✅ PLACEHOLDER — Compare a PlaceholderAPI value

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]PLUGIN INTEGRATION[/COLOR][/B]
✅ VOTIFIER_PLUS — Progress quests from votes

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55AAFF] REWARDS [/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

✅ [B]COMMAND[/B] — Execute one or more console commands
✅ [B]EXP_POINTS / EXP_LEVELS[/B] — Grant experience
✅ [B]MONEY[/B] — Economy rewards through Vault
✅ [B]POINTS[/B] — PlayerPoints rewards
✅ [B]NONE[/B] — Completion without a direct reward

Quest rewards support dynamic values such as quest name, required amount, current progress, and reward amount.

Each period can have independent quest rewards, category-completion rewards, and an all-quests-completed reward. Daily rewards never trigger Weekly or Monthly rewards, and vice versa.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#F5A623]COMMANDS[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]PLAYER COMMANDS[/COLOR][/B]
✅ [B]/dq me [daily|weekly|monthly][/B] — Open your quests for a period
✅ [B]/dq show [period] <category>[/B] — Browse a period's quest category
✅ [B]/dq reroll [period] <index>[/B] — Reroll a quest within its period

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]PERIOD-AWARE ADMIN COMMANDS[/COLOR][/B]
✅ [B]/dqa complete <player> [period] <index>[/B]
✅ [B]/dqa reroll <player> [period] <index>[/B]
✅ [B]/dqa set <player> [period] <slot> <category> <quest-id>[/B]
✅ [B]/dqa reset quests <player> [period|all][/B]
✅ [B]/dqa show <player> [period][/B]
✅ [B]/dqa open <player> [period][/B]

[B][COLOR=#55AAFF]OTHER ADMIN TOOLS[/COLOR][/B]
✅ [B]/dqa reload[/B]
✅ [B]/dqa add / remove / customcomplete[/B]
✅ [B]/dqa convert[/B] — Convert supported storage formats

Existing command formats without a period continue to work. Command and subcommand aliases are configurable.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55AAFF] INTEGRATIONS [/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B]No dependency is required for the core quest system.[/B] Install an optional plugin only when you use its related feature:

✅ PlaceholderAPI
✅ Vault
✅ PlayerPoints
✅ Citizens
✅ WorldGuard
✅ HeadDatabase
✅ Nexo
✅ VotifierPlus
✅ eco

[COLOR=#FFAA00][B]Difference from the archived original:[/B][/COLOR] Version 4.5 has a focused integration set. Legacy hooks for ItemsAdder, Oraxen, MMOItems, RoseStacker, WildStacker, FancyNPCs, MythicMobs, EliteMobs, custom fishing/crate plugins, TokenManager, CoinsEngine, and NuVotifier are not included. The former public Java API/event layer and Folia declaration are also not part of this release.

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#55FFAA] SAFE UPGRADING [/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

Version 4.5 keeps existing Daily-only servers working while adding the new period system:

✅ Existing quest files keep their original names
✅ The previously configured Daily, Weekly, or Monthly period remains the active period
✅ Existing YAML, SQLite, and MySQL player data is migrated into that same period automatically
✅ Existing overall lifetime totals and leaderboard behavior are preserved
✅ Weekly and Monthly are disabled by default until you choose to enable them
✅ Disabled-period data is preserved if that period is enabled again later

[COLOR=#FFAA00][B]Always back up the ODailyQuests folder and database before updating.[/B][/COLOR]

[CENTER][COLOR=#555555]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#F5A623]INSTALLATION & SUPPORT[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[LIST=1]
[*]Run [B]Paper 26.2[/B] with [B]Java 25[/B].
[*]Place [B]ODailyQuests-4.5.jar[/B] in your server's plugins folder.
[*]Start once to generate the configuration and example quest files.
[*]Stop the server, configure the files in [B]plugins/ODailyQuests[/B], then restart.
[*]Enable and configure Weekly or Monthly under [B]quest_periods[/B] when desired.
[/LIST]

